{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2128","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Recycling Center"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the recycling center, there are $$$n$$$ trash bags, the $$$i$$$-th bag has a weight of $$$a_i$$$. At each second, two actions will happen successively: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" First, you must choose a trash bag and destroy it. It will cost $$$1$$$ coin if the weight of the trash bag is strictly greater than $$$c$$$, and it will cost $$$0$$$ coins otherwise. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Then, the weight of each remaining trash bag will get multiplied by two. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"kind":"text","text":" What is the minimum number of coins you have to spend to get rid of all trash bags?"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 1000$$$). The description of the test cases follows. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$c$$$ ($$$1 \\leq n \\leq 30$$$, $$$1 \\leq c \\leq 10^9)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each test case contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$ ($$$1 \\leq a_i \\leq 10^9$$$) — the weight of each trash bag."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, you must output a single integer — the minimum number of coins you have to spend to destroy all trash bags."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n5 10\n10 4 15 1 8\n3 42\n1000000000 1000000000 1000000000\n10 30\n29 25 2 12 15 42 14 6 16 9\n10 1000000\n1 1 1 1 1 1 1 1 1 864026633\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n3\n6\n1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the following explanation: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Numbers in blue represent trash bags that have been destroyed for free, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Numbers in red represent trash bags that have been destroyed for $$$1$$$ coin, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Numbers in black represent trash bags that have not been destroyed yet. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, one solution is: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[10, 4, 15, 1, 8]$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[\\color{blue}{10}, 8, 30, 2, 16]$$$, $$$10$$$ is destroyed for free because $$$10 \\leq 10$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[\\color{blue}{10}, \\color{blue}{8}, 60, 4, 32]$$$, $$$8$$$ is destroyed for free because $$$8 \\leq 10$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[\\color{blue}{10}, \\color{blue}{8}, 120, 8, \\color{red}{32}]$$$, $$$32$$$ is destroyed for $$$1$$$ coin because $$$32 \\gt 10$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[\\color{blue}{10}, \\color{blue}{8}, 240, \\color{blue}{8}, \\color{red}{32}]$$$, $$$8$$$ is destroyed for free because $$$8 \\leq 10$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[\\color{blue}{10}, \\color{blue}{8}, \\color{red}{240}, \\color{blue}{8}, \\color{red}{32}]$$$, $$$240$$$ is destroyed for $$$1$$$ coin because $$$240 \\gt 10$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In total, you paid $$$2$$$ coins, and we can prove it is optimal."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, one solution is: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[1\\,000\\,000\\,000, 1\\,000\\,000\\,000, 1\\,000\\,000\\,000]$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[\\color{red}{1\\,000\\,000\\,000}, 2\\,000\\,000\\,000, 2\\,000\\,000\\,000]$$$, $$$1\\,000\\,000\\,000$$$ is destroyed for $$$1$$$ coin because $$$1\\,000\\,000\\,000 \\gt 42$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[\\color{red}{1\\,000\\,000\\,000}, \\color{red}{2\\,000\\,000\\,000}, 4\\,000\\,000\\,000]$$$, $$$2\\,000\\,000\\,000$$$ is destroyed for $$$1$$$ coin because $$$2\\,000\\,000\\,000 \\gt 42$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[\\color{red}{1\\,000\\,000\\,000}, \\color{red}{2\\,000\\,000\\,000}, \\color{red}{4\\,000\\,000\\,000}]$$$, $$$4\\,000\\,000\\,000$$$ is destroyed for $$$1$$$ coin because $$$4\\,000\\,000\\,000 \\gt 42$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"2128A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2128/problem/A"}